&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;div&gt;Wrike is the most powerful work management platform. Built for teams and organizations looking to collaborate, create, and exceed every day, Wrike brings everyone and all work into a single place to remove complexity, increase productivity, and free people up to focus on their most purposeful work.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our vision:&amp;nbsp; &lt;/strong&gt;A world where everyone is free to focus on their most purposeful work, together.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Location: East Coast&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Wrike is looking for a driven, hands-on Sales Manager to lead our AMS Commercial Sales Team, overseeing both new business acquisition and expansion within our existing customer base. This is a high-impact leadership role focused on building a winning sales culture, driving predictable revenue, and scaling growth across a large, high-value install base.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Impact:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’ll manage and develop a team of Commercial Account Executives and Account Managers, partnering closely with Marketing, RevOps, Customer Success, Solutions Consulting, and executive leadership to execute a strong land-and-expand strategy. If you thrive in fast-paced environments, love coaching talented sellers, and enjoy navigating complex commercial deals, we want to talk to you.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;About the Team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You will lead the AMS Commercial Sales team, responsible for driving revenue across a defined set of Commercial accounts (250 - 1000 employees), including both net-new logos and expansion opportunities within existing Wrike customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reporting to the Manager of AMS Commercial Sales, you’ll enable your team to deeply understand customer pain points, articulate Wrike’s value, and deliver solutions that drive long-term growth and customer satisfaction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Your Impact:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead, coach, and develop a high-performing team of Commercial Account Executives and Account Managers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own new business and expansion revenue targets across the AMS Commercial segment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive pipeline generation, deal execution, and accurate forecasting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Forecast revenue weekly to sales leadership and maintain strong forecast hygiene&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Champion a strategic land-and-expand motion to maximize customer lifetime value&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Inspect deals, coach to close, and actively participate in complex negotiations and escalations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure consistent execution of sales process, methodology, and playbooks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assess sales performance, identify opportunities for improvement, and implement action plans&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner cross-functionally with Marketing, RevOps, Customer Success, Legal, Channel Partners, and Professional Services&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead territory planning, demand generation, deal strategy development, and trend analysis&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hire, onboard, ramp, and retain top sales talent&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive a culture of accountability, urgency, and continuous improvement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Moderate travel as needed (approximately 25%)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Your Qualifications:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of sales management experience (Commercial or Mid-Market preferred)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of overall sales experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record of consistently hitting or exceeding team revenue targets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing both net-new and expansion sales motions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong coaching mindset with hands-on deal leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Data-driven approach to forecasting, pipeline management, and performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to lead in a fast-growth, evolving sales environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’ll Stand Out If You Have&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;SaaS or recurring revenue experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience selling multi-product or platform solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to manage complex, multi-stakeholder sales cycles&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong executive presence and credibility with senior customer stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analytical skills to identify trends, risks, and opportunities in complex deals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with modern sales tech (CRM, forecasting, enablement tools)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why Join Wrike?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible Time Off (FTO)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Company 401(k) Match&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Parental Leave: 18 Weeks Maternity / 4 Week Paternity&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
