&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Education &amp;amp; Experience:&lt;/strong&gt; B.S. in Computer Science, Software Engineering, or equivalent experience; 3+ years as a Sales/Solutions Engineer AND 5+ years in project management or consulting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical Acumen:&lt;/strong&gt; Proven experience working with APIs for software integrations and automating complex workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Consultative Communication:&lt;/strong&gt; Exceptional presentation and objection-handling skills, with a track record of effectively engaging everyone from technical teams to executive stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Process Mastery:&lt;/strong&gt; Ability to quickly dissect a customer&#39;s complex business processes and map them to clear, goal-oriented Wrike implementations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Domain Expertise:&lt;/strong&gt; Deep understanding of change management principles and thorough expertise in at least one key segment (e.g., PMO, Marketing/Creative, IT, or Professional Services).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Execution &amp;amp; Ownership:&lt;/strong&gt; Superior personal organization and a firm sense of accountability to juggle multiple competing priorities with poise under pressure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Standout Qualities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An advanced degree (MBA, MS, or equivalent).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Formal certifications in industry-standard project management methodologies (Agile, PMI, Lean, etc.).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience driving impact within a fast-paced SaaS environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced capability to position Wrike seamlessly into highly complex, integrated enterprise ecosystems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team Dynamics:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will join a collaborative, high-energy team of technical experts and strategic consultants. This role requires close, cross-functional partnership with Sales, Marketing, and Product Management to enhance Wrike&#39;s competitive edge. You will step into a culture that values mentorship, open feedback, and a &quot;people-first&quot; mindset, where you will be empowered to take full ownership of your work while supporting the growth of your peers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Work Style:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are problem solvers who thrive on curiosity and continuous learning. In this role, you will be deeply embedded in our own platform—using Wrike, Salesforce, and modern integration tools to manage your book of business. What sets this position apart from competitors is the true hybrid nature of the work: you aren&#39;t just selling the vision, and you aren&#39;t just implementing it—you are the strategic thread that connects a customer&#39;s initial pain point to their long-term digital transformation success.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why Join Wrike?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;18 calendar days of paid vacation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;12 days of National &amp;amp; Festival holidays (10 fixed, 2 flexible)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sick Leave Compensation (5 Paid Uncertified Sick Days)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Menstrual Leave: Twelve (12) days per calendar year. Women employees are eligible for up to 1 day of menstrual leave per month.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Parental Leave: 26 Weeks Maternity / 4 Week Paternity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2 Volunteer Days&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Group Medical Insurance (Employees + Dependents)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Term Life Insurance (Rs 50,00,000)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Personal Accident Insurance (Rs 50,00,000)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monthly Broadband / Internet Reimbursement (INR 1500)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hybrid Working Model + Complimentary Lunch &amp;amp; Snacks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
